{"id":"prepositions-0107","taskId":"prepositions","title":"Drill set 107","text":null,"source":"drill","gaps":[{"answer":"at","accept":[],"options":[],"base":null,"keyword":null,"lead":null,"sentence":"She smiled ___ the waiter and ordered tea.","hint":"smile ___ sb","explanation":"smile AT somebody."},{"answer":"at","accept":[],"options":[],"base":null,"keyword":null,"lead":null,"sentence":"He\u0027s very good ___ solving puzzles.","hint":"good ___ doing","explanation":"good/bad/brilliant AT an activity."},{"answer":"on","accept":[],"options":[],"base":null,"keyword":null,"lead":null,"sentence":"She blamed the delay ___ the courier company.","hint":"blame sth ___ sb","explanation":"blame something ON somebody = blame somebody FOR something."},{"answer":"with","accept":[],"options":[],"base":null,"keyword":null,"lead":null,"sentence":"Don\u0027t argue ___ your brother about silly things.","hint":"argue ___ sb about sth","explanation":"argue WITH a person ABOUT a topic. \u0027With\u0027 also accepted after argue for a point."},{"answer":"at","accept":[],"options":[],"base":null,"keyword":null,"lead":null,"sentence":"She glanced ___ her watch and stood up.","hint":"glance ___ sth","explanation":"glance AT = look quickly at."},{"answer":"with","accept":[],"options":["at","with","to","from"],"base":null,"keyword":null,"lead":null,"sentence":"I\u0027m not familiar ___ this software yet.","hint":"familiar ___ something","explanation":"\u0027Familiar with\u0027 = knowing something well."},{"answer":"of","accept":[],"options":[],"base":null,"keyword":null,"lead":null,"sentence":"She\u0027s very fond ___ her nieces.","hint":"fond ___ sb/sth","explanation":"fond OF somebody/something."},{"answer":"after","accept":[],"options":[],"base":null,"keyword":null,"lead":null,"sentence":"Could you look ___ my plants while I\u0027m away?","hint":"look ___ = take care of","explanation":"look AFTER somebody/something = take care of them."}]}